UID:28113-1790730000-1790902799@www.lotusfest.org
SUMMARY:Conversations in Bloom: A Symposium on Arts\, Community\, and Memory
DESCRIPTION:Tickets on Sale 8/8\n\nSeptember 30 – October 1\, 2026\nTwo-day Event Cost: $37 ($35 + processing fees) / Student Discount $11 ($9 + processing fees)\nThis event spans 2 days at 3 venues. Wednesday\, 9/30/26 from 9:00 AM – Midnight and Thursday\, 10/1/26 from 9:00 AM – 6:30 PM.\n\nLocation\n\nThe iFell Gallery – 415 W. Fourth Street Bloomington\, IN 47404\nFAR Center for Contemporary Arts – 202 S Rogers St\, Bloomington\, IN 47404\nCicada Cinema – 615 N. Fairview St\, Suite 1\, Bloomington\, IN 47404\n\nLotus is hosting a series of conversations about the crucial role that the arts play in building our communities and identities. Conversations in Bloom: A Symposium on Arts\, Community\, and Memory invites participants to consider how the arts help us make sense of the world around us\, connect individual and collective experience\, and understand the communities we share. \nThis event is ticketed and open to the public. A detailed schedule of events and speakers is coming soon! \nWhat can you expect?\nConversation and dialogue are the beating hearts of this symposium. We have designed the program around a summer-long collaborative planning process with an emphasis on open and interactive session formats. On both days\, the symposium offers an “UnConferencing” space for attendees and presenters to share questions\, ideas\, and feedback with one another. \nSymposium sessions will engage with themes such as: \n\nCreative Placemaking: Community Projects and Renovating Spaces\nStorytelling and Our Shared Futures\nCultivating Intergenerational Collaboration in Arts and Culture\nThe Role of Global Arts Education in Our Communities\nCreative Aging and Folk Arts Practice\n\nTo conclude the program we invite you to attend a keynote session with Michael Orlove (National Endowment for the Arts) and Dr. John Fenn III (American Folklife Center) \nConversations in Bloom is intended to be both a forum for shared reflection and a space for professional development. Participants will discuss the opportunities and challenges of activating\, celebrating\, and preserving community culture through the arts\, while also considering how personal\, institutional\, and communal histories are interwoven into the fabric of Bloomington’s cultural life. \nWho will be there?\nCommunity partners for this event include: Cicada Cinema\, Blueline Media\, MDWST Fable\, Black Vulture Project\, Monroe County History Center\, Exodus Refugee\, Traditional Arts Indiana\, Indiana University Arts and Humanities Council\, Indiana University Center for the Study of Global Change\, Indiana University Department of Folklore and Ethnomusicology…and most importantly YOU!
URL:https://www.lotusfest.org/event/conversations-in-bloom-a-symposium-on-arts-community-and-memory/
LOCATION:IN
CATEGORIES:Lotus Event
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/webp:https://www.lotusfest.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/conversations-in-bloom.webp
END:VEVENT
